The Human Side of Cybersecurity

Welcome to Our First Issue

Every great security story starts with people — not firewalls, not encryption keys, not threat feeds. People.
That’s why I’m thrilled to welcome you to the very first issue of The Human Side of Cybersecurity, a newsletter dedicated to exploring how human behavior, culture, psychology, and everyday habits shape our digital safety.

Cybersecurity isn’t just a technical discipline; it’s a human one.
Behind every breach is a decision, a distraction, a moment of trust, or a clever manipulation. And behind every strong security culture is awareness, empathy, and shared responsibility.

In this issue — and every issue to come — we’ll dive into stories, insights, and practical guidance that help us understand not just what threats exist, but why people fall for them and how we can build safer digital habits together.

Whether you’re a security professional, a curious learner, or someone who just wants to stay safer online, you’re in the right place.

Let’s explore the human side of cybersecurity — one insight at a time.

